# §Fase 124.b — vendored source is stored and checked out BYTE-FOR-BYTE.
#
# `axon-csys/c-src/vendor/` holds third-party cryptography inside the FIPS
# module boundary, pinned by SHA-256 in `PROVENANCE.toml` and verified on every
# build by `axon-csys/tests/vendor_provenance.rs`.
#
# Those hashes are of the bytes UPSTREAM PUBLISHED. Git's automatic
# line-ending conversion would rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout under Windows,
# producing files that differ from upstream by every line — and the gate would
# fail on a clean clone and in CI, reporting tampering where there was none,
# which is the fastest way to teach someone to disable the gate.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion for this tree. It is also the semantically
# correct answer: vendored source that has been reformatted, even invisibly, is
# no longer the implementation whose lineage its header claims.
axon-csys/c-src/vendor/** -text

# The provenance manifest is ours, not upstream's, and may follow normal rules.
axon-csys/c-src/vendor/PROVENANCE.toml text
